The explanation:

1.the line " #include <iostream> " is a header file library, like telling your C++ program: "Hey, I want to be able to rwead input and ptint output." It pulls in a ready-made bundle of code, so you don't have to write all that plumbing yourself.
2.the sentence " using namespace std " means that we can use names for objects and variabeles from the standard library or 
    ^ the standard libary is a massive collection of pre-written code comes with C++. It includes everything you need for common tasks
      like; Input/output (cout, cin), datastructures (vector, map, string), math function (sqrt, pow), and file operationss, and much more.
